Which release doesn't boot ?<br>I just flashed my DM-1801 with the stable release of Feb 28th (using the Python script), and it works.<br><br>You're talking about XPresso, what about NXP SDK version ?<br>About my comment about newlib, that was about external build process, using Makefile.<br>We are using redlib because it's small, really small, and the remaining space is getting tight.<br>You can do whatever you want, but don't expect any support from us if you're not following the only guaranteed way to compile the firmware.<br><br><strong class="text-strong">EDIT</strong>: I just recompiled a firmware for the DM-1801, using the latest released source files, then flashed. It works as expected.<br><strong class="text-strong">EDIT 2</strong>: I've done the same with the Japanese version, and it work as well.<br><br><br>Thanks.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Mar 15, 2022 1:31 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
